-- title:
--   Integrality of the X₀(p) two-chart model over an unramified DVR
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $O$ be a discrete valuation ring that is an integral domain whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $p$, i.e. $\mathfrak{m}_O = (p)$ as an ideal of $O$. Let $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldFull p` be the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q} \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,\mathbb{Q}$ obtained by adjoining to $\mathbb{Q}$ the family `divisorExpansions p`, and let $j =$ `IgusaScheme.jFull p` be the distinguished element of $F$ given by the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant. Write $\mathfrak{X} =$ `DRModel p` for the scheme [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel ℤ F j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout gluing $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra `chartAlg ℤ F {j}` of $F$ to $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra `chartAlg ℤ F {j⁻¹}` along the maps `fFin`, `fInf`, and let `DRModel.toBase p` $: \mathfrak{X} \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}$ be the structure morphism obtained by descending the two maps induced by the structure morphisms $\mathbb{Z} \to$ `chartAlg ℤ F {j}` and $\mathbb{Z} \to$ `chartAlg ℤ F {j⁻¹}`. The assertion is that the fibre product of `DRModel.toBase p` with the morphism $\operatorname{Spec} O \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}$ induced by $\mathbb{Z} \to O$ is an integral scheme, i.e. nonempty, irreducible and reduced.
--
--   This is the integrality of the base change to $O$ of the two-chart integral model of $X_0(p)$ over $\mathbb{Z}$ (the Deligne–Rapoport model, in the unramified case $\mathfrak{m}_O = (p)$). It is the input used by the subsequent analysis of the model over $O$ — regularity of local rings, the branch ideals at the two chart origins and the identification of the generic point of the base change.
